 ## Operating characteristics
-- **Time Complexity:** Reconstruction time scales linearly with the number of selected ranks $r_k$. Progressive decoding allows for early termination or lower-quality previews by using smaller $r_k$.
-- **Memory Complexity:** Storage is determined by the full Tucker decomposition ($R_1 R_2 R_3 + \sum I_k R_k$). Progressive reconstruction does not reduce storage but allows variable-quality access.
